The board's ALSA hooks for OH 7.0's audio HDI (vendor/oneplus 0003 turns its ALSA mode on), written for the OnePlus 6.
The port's audio_alsa files were the rk3568 templates (rk809 controls "Playback Path", "DACL Playback Volume"), so
nothing could route sound on this card.

- playback: MultiMedia1 (hw:0,0) to the quaternary MI2S port and the MAX98927 speaker amplifier
  ("QUAT_MI2S_RX Audio Mixer MultiMedia1"); volume is the amplifier's "Speaker Volume" (0-6, set to 5 at init: it
  resets to 0, silent); the headset path (WCD9340) is not set up, every output pin uses the speaker
- capture: the main microphone, WCD9340 ADC3 through decimator 0 and SLIMbus TX0 into MultiMedia2 (hw:0,1);
  "ADC3 Volume". q6asm gives each front end one DSP session, so a capture on MultiMedia1 fails while it plays
  ("Audio Client already active"). CaptureGetSceneDev returns 0: the adapter takes the first device after it
- routes are set in Init, which the adapter calls right after snd_pcm_open: its snd_pcm_hw_params also prepares the
  stream, and a front end with no route fails prepare ("ASoC: no backend DAIs enabled for MultiMedia1"). They stay
  on (DAPM powers a path only while a stream runs)
- capture periods of 20 ms: the adapter reads one ALSA period per call and the HDI fails a read larger than the
  caller's buffer; audio_server reads 40 ms at a time and the adapter's default period is 100 ms (capped at 16 KB)
- signatures as OH 7.0's alsa_snd_render.h / alsa_snd_capture.h declare them; elements are looked up by name
  (numid 0: SndElementItemInit leaves numid unset)

Measured with tinyplay/tinycap: a 1 kHz tone on the speaker records at -18.6 dBFS on ADC3. Through OH (an OHAudio
renderer and an OHAudio capturer, with drivers/peripheral 0001): -34.3 and -25.4 dBFS in two runs.

